SUMMARY:Fall Hike at Penny's Bend Nature Preserve
DESCRIPTION:Experience the beauty of autumn at Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, an 84-acre natural area in northeast Durham managed by the North Carolina Botanical Garden. Surrounded on three sides by the Eno River\, this unique preserve protects mature forests\, open prairies\, and populations of regionally rare plants. Explore the fall landscape while learning about Penny’s Bend’s distinctive natural communities and how the Garden’s stewardship helps conserve this ecologically significant preserve. This program counts toward the field trip requirement for the Certificate in Native Plants program. \nFee: $20 ($18 Members) \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fall-hike-pennys-bend/
LOCATION:Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, Old Oxford Rd\, Durham\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours,Learn
GEO:36.0860873;-78.8475216
